# Line endings are LF everywhere.
#
# `.editorconfig` already declares `end_of_line = lf`, but that is only a convention an editor
# may honour. Several build gates are byte-exact: they regenerate an artefact and compare it to
# the committed copy (`npm run tokens:check`, `npm run contracts:check`). On a Windows checkout
# with `core.autocrlf=true` and no attributes file, git hands those gates a CRLF copy of an LF
# blob, so the gate fails with "STALE" even though nothing drifted. Declaring the rule here makes
# every clone produce the same bytes the generator produced.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only entry points keep CRLF if they are ever added.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be text-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
